Fixed all three findings.

- `src/runtime.rs`: `in` now uses a membership-specific comparison, so date/duration vs number returns `yes`/`no` while decimal/number mixing still errors. List comparison now scans unequal-length lists instead of stopping at the shorter one.
- `src/decimal.rs`: parsing accumulates magnitude as `u128`, and quotient conversion uses the signed-magnitude helper, so negative `i128::MIN` parses and divides correctly.
- Added boundary/regression tests for negative minimum text/quotient, mixed-kind membership, and unequal-length decimal lists.

